# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SMB Website Design Program — .gitignore
#
# Layout: source is tracked; everything generated or private stays local.
# docs/github-handoff.md explains the exact commit steps.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Git plumbing (in case Git is initialized at project root later) ---
.git/

# --- Generated preview output (rebuildable: scripts/generate-preview.js) ---
# dist/ is never source. Generated pages embed prospect records and must not
# be published to the repository even after the records are deleted locally.
dist/

# --- Private business records (real prospects/customers) ---
# records/ is the local-only convention for private PreviewSiteRecord JSON
# files. NEVER track real business records here. Synthetic, commit-safe
# fixtures live in examples/ (preview-site.example.json is intentionally
# empty of real data; preview-site.test-plumbing.json is explicitly labeled
# test-data in its $comment — never for outreach).
# The one tracked exception is records/LOCAL-ONLY.md — the warning sign
# itself stays in the repo so the convention travels with it.
records/*
!records/LOCAL-ONLY.md
*.private.json
*.private.*

# --- Secrets / environment ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*_rsa
*_ed25519
secrets*.json
!secrets.example.json

# --- Dependencies / toolchains (none are committed today, but ignore anyway) ---
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Logs / temp / scratch ---
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
~$*
*.bak
j60_*.txt
j*.txt
probe*.txt
scratch/
out*.txt

# --- Browser-test artifacts (headless Edge profiles, screenshots, dumps) ---
test-artifacts/
screenshots/
.cdp/
*.png
*.jpg.tmp

# --- OS / editor junk ---
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# --- Editors / IDE ---
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Workshop agent state (per-machine context, not project source) ---
.workshop/

# --- Agent task-tracking bundles (per-machine planning state) ---
plans/

# IMPORTANT: .gitignore does NOT affect files Git already tracks.
# Before the first commit, confirm with:
#   git ls-files --  .
# (Expected: empty before handoff. See docs/github-handoff.md.)
